Subject: [PATCH] kwvk: mark host-visible memory HOST_CACHED

trynix carries this patch for kwvk, unkernel's guest Vulkan driver,
until unkernel takes it (pithings/unkernel#32, change 7).

DDNet asks for HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_CACHED for every buffer it maps
(src/engine/client/backend/vulkan/backend_vulkan.cpp), and its
FindMemoryType returns type 0 when nothing matches. kwvk's host-visible
type was HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT, so DDNet allocated device-only
memory, failed to map it, and gave up:

  E gfx: Failed to initialize graphics. Out of ideas.

That memory is a malloc'd shadow in the guest's RAM, so reads of it
are cached, and type 1 now says so.

---
diff --git a/vk/icd/icd.c b/vk/icd/icd.c
index 169e442..5d10c44 100644
--- a/vk/icd/icd.c
+++ b/vk/icd/icd.c
@@ -489,7 +489,10 @@ static void pd_init(struct kw_physical_device *pd, struct kw_reply *rep)
 	m->memoryTypeCount = 2;
 	m->memoryTypes[0].propertyFlags = VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT;
 	m->memoryTypes[0].heapIndex = 0;
-	m->memoryTypes[1].propertyFlags = VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT | VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT;
+	/* the shadow is the guest's own RAM, so reads of it are cached (DDNet
+	 * asks for HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_CACHED for every buffer it maps) */
+	m->memoryTypes[1].propertyFlags =
+		VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT | VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT | VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT;
 	m->memoryTypes[1].heapIndex = 1;
 }
 
